# Who is asked to review what. See GOVERNANCE.md.
#
# Each project profile has one line. The maintainers own it. Do not leave a line
# with no owner: GitHub then treats the file as having no code owner at all.
#
# Profile reviewers are NOT listed here (GOVERNANCE.md, Profile reviewers). There
# are two kinds: a representative, who works on the project, and an external
# steward, who has no affiliation with any covered project and looks after the
# profile when no representative is interested. GitHub requires a code owner to
# have write access, and one code owner on a line is enough for GitHub. A code
# owner's approval would then count as the approval of the profile. So their
# reviews are requested by hand, recorded in the pull request, and listed in
# MAINTAINERS.md.
#
# GitHub requests a review from the owners of a file when a pull request is
# ready for review (not while it is a draft). Branch protection decides whether
# that review is required. When it is required, an approval from any one owner
# on the line is enough. GitHub ignores an owner with no write access to this
# repository.

*                                    @mauromorales

# Conflicted files (GOVERNANCE.md, "Bootstrap"). The first maintainer with no
# affiliation to any covered project replaces @mauromorales on these lines as
# the required approver. Adding them next to @mauromorales would not make their
# approval required, because any one owner on a line is enough. GitHub enforces
# only that a code owner approves. The symmetric rule rests on the maintainers
# and the public record. data/lineage.yaml, site/projects_meta.yaml,
# site/content.py and site/drafts/base_choice.yaml state facts about Kairos,
# Hadron and Spectro Cloud next to facts about the other projects. GitHub cannot
# protect one entry of a file, so the whole file is listed. During the
# bootstrap, a change that touches an entry about Kairos, Hadron or Spectro
# Cloud is conflicted. This file and MAINTAINERS.md are listed so that the
# hand-over cannot be undone by one approval. Any other file that states a fact
# about these projects counts the same way. For example site/build.py holds one
# such label, the fleet server name of Kairos. It is code, so it is not listed
# here, and the rule still applies to it. GOVERNANCE.md holds the ownership,
# administrator and removal rules. A change to it is conflicted, and for 24
# months after the bootstrap ends the founder clause in it also needs the
# owner's agreement for the protected text in it.
